/* ================= THE TYPEFACES, EMBEDDED =================

   The game asked for three faces through a Google Fonts `@import` and never received one of them.
   `@import` must precede every other rule in a stylesheet; it sat on line 8, under
   `*,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box}`, so every browser silently dropped it. Measured on
   the shipped build: ZERO requests to fonts.googleapis.com, `document.fonts` empty. Cinzel is on
   every button, tag, display heading and tab label; Cormorant Garamond is the body; IM Fell English
   is `.hand`, which is the parchment ledger's whole voice. All three had been falling back to bare
   `serif` and Georgia since the day they were added.

   `document.fonts.check("16px 'Cinzel'")` returns TRUE for a font that was never requested — the
   spec assumes an unlisted family is a system font — so the one API you would reach for to test
   this confirms the bug is absent. The honest test is whether a request is made at all.

   They are embedded rather than re-linked. The build already writes an offline shell (service
   worker, precached manifest) and its own banner said "no internet needed except optional fonts";
   linking them would have traded a silent bug for a load-time network dependency in an app that
   is meant to run without one.

   WHAT IS IN HERE, and why it is this small: only the faces the stylesheet actually names —
   Cinzel (variable, 400-900, one file for all three weights), Cormorant Garamond upright
   (variable 300-700) and italic, and IM Fell English ITALIC only, because `.hand` is the one rule
   that uses it and it never asks for the upright. Google's `latin` subset only: its range already
   covers Latin-1, and the game's entire non-ASCII vocabulary is 26 characters, all of them in its
   own tables. Subset to 214 codepoints — printable ASCII, those 26, and Latin-1 for a house name
   somebody types. 273KB of woff2 down to 119KB, 145KB of it dropped as faces nothing renders.

   A few ornaments the game writes are not in these faces and never were — U+2726 BLACK FOUR
   POINTED STAR is in none of the three — so the browser falls back for that glyph alone, which is
   exactly what it did before. Nothing regresses.

   LICENCE. All three are SIL Open Font License 1.1, which permits embedding:
     Cinzel             (c) Natanael Gama                      https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Cinzel
     Cormorant Garamond (c) Christian Thalmann, Catharsis Fonts https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Cormorant+Garamond
     IM Fell English    (c) Igino Marini                        https://fonts.google.com/specimen/IM+Fell+English
   The OFL requires the notice to travel with the font; it travels in this comment and in README.
   ================================================================= */


export const FONT_CINZEL = "data:font/woff2;base64,";

export const FONT_CORMORANT = "data:font/woff2;base64,";

export const FONT_CORMORANT_ITALIC = "data:font/woff2;base64,";

export const FONT_IMFELL_ITALIC = "data:font/woff2;base64,";
